e>Getchell</surname><given-names>WS</given-names></name><name><surname>Larsen</surname><given-names>GC</given-names></name><name><surname>Morris</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name><name><surname>McAnulty</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Epidemiology of syncope in hospitalized patients</article-title><source>J Gen Intern Med</source><year>1999</year><volume>14</volume><issue>11</issue><fpage>677</fpage><lpage>687</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1525-1497.1999.03199.x</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10571716</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR20"><label>20.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Colivicchi</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Ammirati</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Melina</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Development and prospective validation of a risk stratification system for patients with syncope in the emergency department: the OESIL risk score</article-title><source>Eur Heart J</source><year>2003</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>811</fpage><lpage>819</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0195-668X(02)00827-8</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12727148</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn><p>Disclaimer: The views expressed in this paper are those of the author(s) and not those of the editors, editorial board or publisher.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>